1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,479
Welcome to RelayProof.

2
00:00:01,479 --> 00:00:08,547
This is a complete walkthrough of the current audio
and video prototype: how publishers issue signed

3
00:00:08,547 --> 00:00:15,190
media records, how recipients verify exact files,
what Chromaprint can and cannot tell us, how

4
00:00:15,190 --> 00:00:21,551
transcript and video review works, and how to use
the Chrome extension with a YouTube tab.

5
00:00:21,551 --> 00:00:25,777
The central idea is evidence, not a magic
authenticity score.

6
00:00:25,777 --> 00:00:28,031
Each result has a narrow meaning.

7
00:00:28,031 --> 00:00:31,482
Missing evidence is not proof that a clip is fake.

8
00:00:31,482 --> 00:00:33,270
Start in the Issue workflow.

9
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:39,759
Choose an audio or video file up to one hundred
twenty eight megabytes, enter a publisher name and

10
00:00:39,759 --> 00:00:43,335
asset title, then make a declaration about its
origin.

11
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:50,090
RelayProof computes a SHA two fifty six digest in
the browser and signs the claim with a local E C D S

12
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:50,487
A key.

13
00:00:50,487 --> 00:00:55,189
You can download the signed sidecar and share it
with the original file.

14
00:00:55,189 --> 00:01:01,877
An optional Chromaprint checkbox adds a fingerprint
reference, but only if the local media service is

15
00:01:01,877 --> 00:01:02,407
running.

16
00:01:02,407 --> 00:01:07,705
If the file is a video, that fingerprint covers the
audio track, not the picture.

17
00:01:07,705 --> 00:01:11,560
In Verify, load the media and its RelayProof
sidecar.

18
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:19,049
First, the signature check asks whether the signed
fields still match the public key embedded in that

19
00:01:19,049 --> 00:01:19,642
sidecar.

20
00:01:19,642 --> 00:01:22,163
It does not prove who owns the key.

21
00:01:22,163 --> 00:01:29,133
Next, the exact file check compares the file's SHA
two fifty six digest with the signed digest.

22
00:01:29,133 --> 00:01:31,876
A match means these exact bytes match.

23
00:01:31,876 --> 00:01:37,215
Re-encoding normally changes them, so a mismatch is
not proof of forgery.

24
00:01:37,215 --> 00:01:43,295
Pinning a key is only a local reminder on this
device, not an identity certificate.

25
00:01:43,295 --> 00:01:46,854
Older RelayProof audio sidecars remain supported.

26
00:01:46,854 --> 00:01:51,661
Chromaprint is an optional candidate-matching aid
for near-identical audio.

27
00:01:51,661 --> 00:01:56,533
When issuing, RelayProof can sign a compressed
fingerprint into the sidecar.

28
00:01:56,533 --> 00:02:00,755
Later, a recipient can compare a different file to
that reference.

29
00:02:00,755 --> 00:02:07,316
The local pyacoustid service returns a similarity
score after aligning fingerprints; it does not look

30
00:02:07,316 --> 00:02:09,330
up tracks or publishers online.

31
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:13,228
Generation uses at most the first one hundred twenty
seconds.

32
00:02:13,228 --> 00:02:19,918
There is no calibrated threshold, and a high score
does not authenticate a publisher, prove a claim, or

33
00:02:19,918 --> 00:02:21,023
detect A I audio.

34
00:02:21,023 --> 00:02:27,454
It is especially important to test short speech
clips and real re-encodes before relying on a score.

35
00:02:27,454 --> 00:02:31,798
The Review page handles content review separately
from provenance.

36
00:02:31,798 --> 00:02:37,078
You can play local audio or video, paste a
transcript, or import subtitle files.

37
00:02:37,078 --> 00:02:43,494
If the self-hosted Whisper service is installed, you
can ask it to transcribe the selected media.

38
00:02:43,494 --> 00:02:49,910
The text pre-check uses limited English phrase
rules, flags selected risk language, and surfaces

39
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:52,784
numeric or date claims for source checking.

40
00:02:52,784 --> 00:02:59,267
It does not fetch official records, verify facts,
confirm a speaker's registration, inspect every

41
00:02:59,267 --> 00:03:03,077
frame, or decide whether a clip complies with SEBI
rules.

42
00:03:03,077 --> 00:03:07,288
A human reviewer must check context and current
primary sources.

43
00:03:07,288 --> 00:03:13,611
For video, the Review page can also sample up to
twenty four evenly spaced frames across the clip.

44
00:03:13,611 --> 00:03:19,935
The browser scales and captures still images, then
sends only those selected stills to your local

45
00:03:19,935 --> 00:03:23,194
Tesseract service after you click the scan button.

46
00:03:23,194 --> 00:03:29,713
English text is returned with timestamps; clicking a
timestamp jumps the video player to that moment.

47
00:03:29,713 --> 00:03:33,560
You can edit the OCR text and include it in the
phrase scan.

48
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:35,581
This is not full-frame coverage.

49
00:03:35,581 --> 00:03:41,383
It can miss brief overlays and misread small,
stylized, low-contrast, or non-English text.

50
00:03:41,383 --> 00:03:43,534
Inspect the entire video manually.

51
00:03:43,534 --> 00:03:48,513
The Chrome extension is an unpacked Manifest version
three prototype.

52
00:03:48,513 --> 00:03:49,684
It has two paths.

53
00:03:49,684 --> 00:03:56,933
First, select a local audio or video file and a
sidecar; the extension can verify the signature and

54
00:03:56,933 --> 00:04:02,498
exact hash locally, then request a candidate
comparison if the bytes differ.

55
00:04:02,498 --> 00:04:09,673
Second, on YouTube or another page, start playback
before opening the popup, load a sidecar with a

56
00:04:09,673 --> 00:04:13,408
Chromaprint reference, and click Start Tab Capture.

57
00:04:13,408 --> 00:04:18,167
Choose fifteen, thirty, or sixty seconds, and keep
the popup open.

58
00:04:18,167 --> 00:04:24,683
The extension captures the sound currently playing;
it does not download the source video.

59
00:04:24,683 --> 00:04:30,248
A tab capture is a new recording, so it cannot
exact-match the original file.

60
00:04:30,248 --> 00:04:31,844
Here is where media goes.

61
00:04:31,844 --> 00:04:36,962
Exact hashing and sidecar signature checks happen in
the browser or extension.

62
00:04:36,962 --> 00:04:43,411
If you opt into fingerprinting or comparison, the
selected media is sent to the self-hosted local

63
00:04:43,411 --> 00:04:43,943
backend.

64
00:04:43,943 --> 00:04:48,330
Whisper transcription sends the full selected clip
to that backend.

65
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:52,652
Video OCR sends only the sampled still images, not
the full video.

66
00:04:52,652 --> 00:04:59,366
The Chrome extension calls the backend on your own
computer, with access restricted to its configured

67
00:04:59,366 --> 00:05:00,762
extension identifier.

68
00:05:00,762 --> 00:05:05,150
The shared preview backend is offline and is not for
private clips.

69
00:05:05,150 --> 00:05:10,867
The service needs native Chromaprint and Tesseract
components for the related features.

70
00:05:10,867 --> 00:05:12,902
A few important boundaries.

71
00:05:12,902 --> 00:05:18,772
RelayProof does not detect whether arbitrary audio
is A I generated or fake.

72
00:05:18,772 --> 00:05:25,346
It does not establish real-world publisher identity,
speaker consent, or claim truth.

73
00:05:25,346 --> 00:05:30,433
Chromaprint is not a watermark and does not compare
video visuals.

74
00:05:30,433 --> 00:05:36,460
The content review is not exhaustive and never
returns a SEBI-approved result.

75
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:43,817
C two P A validation, watermark or S B R recovery,
and Monad anchoring are still not connected.

76
00:05:43,817 --> 00:05:50,704
A valid signature means only that the signed data
checks against the included public key.

77
00:05:50,704 --> 00:05:53,757
Keep each of those distinctions visible.

78
00:05:53,757 --> 00:05:58,922
To try the complete flow, issue a sidecar for a test
audio or video file.

79
00:05:58,922 --> 00:06:04,087
If you want a candidate match, enable the optional
Chromaprint reference.

80
00:06:04,087 --> 00:06:09,970
Install the local Python requirements and native
libraries, then start the backend.

81
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:17,216
For Chrome, load the extension folder as unpacked,
copy its identifier, and configure that identifier

82
00:06:17,216 --> 00:06:19,368
before restarting the backend.

83
00:06:19,368 --> 00:06:26,758
Select the sidecar in the extension, then choose a
local file or capture a short sample from the active

84
00:06:26,758 --> 00:06:27,044
tab.

85
00:06:27,044 --> 00:06:29,197
Review every result cautiously.

86
00:06:29,197 --> 00:06:33,429
RelayProof is a developing evidence workflow, not an
oracle.

87
00:06:33,429 --> 00:06:36,586
Evidence first; verdicts never without proof.
